<title>USA: Procter &amp; Gamble to continue shr buyback.</title>
<headline>Procter &amp; Gamble to continue shr buyback.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Procter &amp; Gamble Co said Tuesday it plans to continue repurchasing its outstanding common stock through the 1997-98 fiscal year, and expects its investments to be in the range of $1.0 billion.</p>
<p>In addition, the company said it will continue the buyback program initiated in 1995 to offset per share earnings dilution resulting from management compensation programs.</p>
<p>The company also said it expects to be able to proceed with desired strategic acquisitions in addition to the stock repurchase program.</p>
</text>
